NAME
       klog - read the kernel log

SYNOPSIS
       int cervus_klog(char *buf, int size);
       int cervus_dbg_print(const char *msg);

DESCRIPTION
       Copies the kernel ring buffer into BUF. Messages carry a level;
       the runtime threshold decides which reach the serial port and
       can be changed from the debug console.

RETURN VALUE
       The number of bytes copied, or negative on failure.

       dbg_print writes one line straight into the kernel log, which is
       how a program leaves a trace that survives even when its own
       output is lost.

SEE ALSO
       dmesg(1), vt(2)
